title Constel dev-net ledger r1 — the fake net runs the real Mycelium supply law, its money moving only by the identity that holds its genesis
prompt Keep taking the next agent-doable Lindy-first crux; approve own design rounds; double-seat; send each increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates.
think The Constel dev-net harness (r1-r4) closed its arc, and its own r4 log + exploration named the next crux plainly: a real settlement/economic test running against a spun-up constel, proving the bench earns its keep — or the Mycelium consensus design read. The dev-net was named the crux of Season D precisely because it is the bench every later Season-D rung runs on. So the highest-Lindy, still-tractable move is to run something real ON it now, not to open a new far module.
think Surveyed the tree: mycelium/fold.rye already carries a real primitive — the myc supply as a pure fold over Kumara-signed facts (Σ issued − Σ taxed, non-negative, an overdraw refusing the whole fold, star reservations draining like tax). It has stood alone since the Build Journey; what it never had was a network to belong to — its facts were signed by a bare demo keypair tied to no settled identity. The dev-net supplies exactly that: a spun-up Constel opens a genesis galaxy whose Deed names a keeper, a real settled identity.
think Verified the composition is honest before writing: settlement and mycelium/fold both import the same tally/kumara.rye, so a fact signed by a settled Deed's keeper verifies against the fold. The galaxy Deed's keeper field is keypair_from_seed(keeper_seed).public_key.bytes (tilak.pubkey_of); mint_fact stores signer.public_key.toBytes(); for Ed25519 those two encodings are equal, so a fact minted by keypair_from_seed(keeper_seed) provably carries galaxy.keeper. That equality is the load-bearing cross-check — asserted in open_ledger.
think The crux fused two promises into one module. First, the quarantine wraps the LEDGER, not only the net: open_ledger opens only through constel_net.spin_up, which refuses UnsafeName before a single genesis — there is no code path to a ledger under an @p-shaped name, so the money is sealed inside the sandbox by the harness's own wall. Second, sovereignty is STRUCTURAL: admit refuses any fact whose signer's key is not galaxy.keeper (NotSovereign) before the log; issue/tax mint sovereign-signed facts. The fold proves a fact is internally honest (someone signed these bytes); the dev-net adds the missing half — whose net this is — turning "a signed fact" into "a fact the net's own identity authorized," exactly as mandate/keyed and tablecloth_keyed bind bytes to a settled point.
obs Landed pond/apps/constel_net_ledger.rye + tools/constel_net_ledger_witness.rish + a pond/apps/mycelium_fold.rye symlink (mirroring how settlement deps are symlinked into pond/apps; the symlinked module's kumara.rye/tally_copy.rye imports resolve to the pond/apps copies already present). Composes constel_net.spin_up + mycelium/fold public API only — invents no storage, weakens no bound.
obs Selftest GREEN first pass (5 cases): a law-safe net opens a ledger whose sovereign IS the genesis keeper (pk == galaxy.keeper asserted, galaxy verifies, fresh supply 0); issue 100 / tax 30 / issue 20 folds to supply 90 over three sovereign facts; an @p-shaped name (sarlev) opens NO ledger (UnsafeName); a tax of 80 over supply 50 refuses Overdraw WHOLE (supply held at 50, log untouched — the Mycelium non-negativity law holds inside the fake net); an alien signer's internally-honest fact refuses NotSovereign before the log (log stays empty). The witness re-runs the harness (constel_net) AND the Mycelium fold GREEN at its door. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0.
obs Reaches no custody gate: the Mycelium fold is a supply MODEL, not a payment rail (gate #3 untouched), and the ledger holds no real key/funds/network (gate #4 the maintainer's own Kumara untouched; a served ledger reaches the serve gate). This is a self-approved design round opened with its own exploration doc, exactly as the harness rungs were.
loom witness=constel_net_ledger_witness cases=5 harness_rerun=green fold_rerun=green build=first_pass
file active-designing/20260813-030005_constel-devnet-ledger-exploration.md the self-approved round: the crux, why bind the ledger to the genesis keeper, four rounds named (r1 sovereign ledger · r2 star reservations · r3 travels · r4 read-true)
file pond/apps/constel_net_ledger.rye r1 — open_ledger (quarantine + sovereign derive + pk==keeper assert), issue/tax (sovereign-signed mint), admit (NotSovereign gate before the fold), supply (fresh fold of the whole log)
file pond/apps/mycelium_fold.rye symlink to mycelium/fold.rye so the ledger folds through the real supply primitive
file tools/constel_net_ledger_witness.rish proves the ledger GREEN (5 cases) and re-runs both the harness and the Mycelium fold at its door
file work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md accreted the ledger r1 landing after the harness arc; next crux points at ledger r2-r4 or the Mycelium consensus design read
recommend keep-going — the fake net now runs the real supply law, so the next agent-doable Lindy-first crux is ledger r2 (star reservations settle beside the topology, draining supply like tax) or the Mycelium consensus design read (over TigerBeetle+Mysticeti); the three breach renames (cairn-first) + deep debride + seed force-push stay Keaton's hand (gates #1/#5)
